00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:05.430 align:start position:0%
good design begins with very basic  elements and once you understand what  these elements are  you can take any motion graphic design  to another level  the elements of art are varied in their  interpretations but for the sake of this  short training we are looking at  line  shape  space  size  form  color  tone  intensity and texture we can think of  these elements as a collection of  abstract building blocks  they can be combined and arranged in any  way we like to create a visual statement  let's start by breaking down lines  a line is a one-dimensional path created  by a point moving in space  they can vary in width  length  and direction  lines help to give alignment which leads  to appeal and order in design  they can indicate a state of rest when  horizontal  signify a sense of height when vertical  imply stability and solidity when  horizontal and vertical or suggest a  sense of movement when diagonal  they lead the eye in a composition and  communicate information through their  direction  lines can exist as elements in  themselves  or they can be used to produce other  elements like shapes  a shape is an element of design that is  usually defined by enclosed lines  it is two-dimensional with height and  width  a shape can be geometric and include  squares  rectangles and circles  or a shape can be organic irregular or  asymmetrical  a singular shape cannot exist without  generating another negative shape  the meeting of two defined shapes  produces a boundary line  the area around the primary object in a  composition is known as negative space  the area occupied by the object of focus  is known as positive space  the relationship between these two can  greatly affect the composition  size is the relationship between one  shape to that of another  differences in size can create  interesting relationships within a  composition  generally to have balance a large shape  requires the existence of a smaller  shape  shapes of equal size create focal  confusion  with the eye not knowing where to focus  by varying the size of the shapes the  eye is drawn to the larger dominant  shape  if the size difference is exaggerated  tension can be created  this tension can be used to add impact  to a composition  a form is an object that exists in space  as an enclosed volume with three  dimensions  height  width and depth examples of geometric  form are found in a cube  sphere  pyramid  or cylinder  a form can also be abstract and flow  freely  color is an element with three main  characteristics  hue  tone and intensity  hue is the descriptive name of color  red  green and blue are the three primary  hues and from these three  all other colors can be created  secondary colors contain a mixture of  two primaries  tertiary colors fall between any primary  color and its adjacent secondary  a tent is any color mixed with white  and a shade is any color mixed with  black  tone is simply the darkness or lightness  of an object  sometimes referred to as value tone is  one of the most powerful design elements  and helps to create different moods  white is the lightest value black is the  darkest  the value halfway between these extremes  is called middle gray  dark colors can suggest a sense of  mystery  light colors can describe a brighter  more energetic mood  in any design the area of highest  contrast between light and dark will  always demand maximum attention  the eye is naturally drawn to the area  of highest tonal contrast  color and tone are unique and separate  elements  all colors have a tone but tone can  exist without color  intensity is the strength of a color  bright colors are often associated with  positive energy and are undiluted  darker colors are more subdued and  create a more serious mood  lastly texture is an important art  element that can bring an extra layer of  depth and appeal to a composition the  use of textures is one of the most  powerful tools for creating compelling  graphic design without relying on the  complexity of many elements  texture can be drawn  painted or photographed  textures evoke emotion and bring life to  design  the contrast of highly textured visual  information and striking flat design is  always a winning strategy  although this list of elements seems  straightforward the more you study  design the more varied the list becomes  some add to the list and some subtract  from it the elements of design are not a  guaranteed recipe for design success but  if you use them correctly they are  extremely useful building blocks for  creating visual design
 

